		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Battery Terminal Checks:</strong> Motorcycle transporters ensure that the battery terminals are clean and securely connected. Insufficient connection can lead to battery failure during transit.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>One-Quarter Tank Fuel Regulation:</strong> To prevent fuel leaks and ensure safe transport, the motorcycle should be filled up to only one-quarter of its tank.</span></li>
